raylib-jlt
----------
  Copyright (c) 2026 Burin Choomnuan (@burinc)
  https://github.com/jlt-commons/raylib-jlt
  Licensed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0.

  This project is a port of raylib-jlt, the raylib bindings for jolt
  written by Burin Choomnuan. The port started from raylib-jlt commit
  ffd97a91727b02c8f2a5ee2c194bfb64d10c2d4a (2026-10-06):

    https://github.com/jlt-commons/raylib-jlt/tree/ffd97a91727b02c8f2a5ee2c194bfb64d10c2d4a

  The module layout, the bindings, the keyword-argument drawing API and the
  color palette come from raylib-jlt. The port replaces jolt.ffi calls with
  babashka.ffi calls and renames the namespaces from net.b12n.raylib.* to
  raylib.*. It also changes parts of the API: structs pass by value as maps,
  meshes, materials, shaders and audio streams are maps instead of native
  pointers, and run! moved to raylib.repl.

  The raylib example programs ported by raylib-jlt live in
  https://github.com/jlt-commons/raylib-jolt-demo.

